dog park, No Dogs are allowed at the Dog Park.\u201d They notice anyone walking by it seems to look away instinctively, but since they are scouting it out the dog goes on point and looks at them.<br /> <br /> Liberty tries throwing a stick over the dog\u2019s head and it retrieves it, bringing it to the fence. They get close enough for the dog to ask them \u201cWhat are you guys doing here?\u201d It is at this point they realize that this dog is not really a dog. It introduces itself as Colin the Guard Dog and is really excited to see them, he\u2019s supposed to be on the eye for intruders and demons, but since they threw a stick for him they can\u2019t be that bad.<br /> <br /> Liberty manages to convince Colin to join them for a little bit and they buy Colin some dog treats. Colin explains that his masters give him better tasting dog treats. He then starts sniffing at Liberty\u2019s leg saying that he smells a little bit like a dog treat and tries to bite him. But isn\u2019t successful at piercing Liberty\u2019s skin.<br /> <br /> It is at this point they realize Colin is a Cryptid with the job of protecting the Infrastructure while the Angels are away. And that the Angels have been using the dog park as a way of holding meetings away from the prying eyes of Mortals. The dog treats given to him are laced with Aether to help train him to attack Demons.<br /> <br /> Alan decides a good idea might be to take the Cryptid to his suborned Infrastructure to get it some Aether. That way it would stop trying to eat them and they could use it to bribe the creature to be on their side.<br /> <br /> After convincing Colin to keep his mouth shut they brought him to Alan\u2019s place of work. When Colin asked where they were and Alan clumsily told him he worked there. Endangering his Cover caused the veins on his hands to look like circuits. He put on some gloves and continued into his suborned Infrastructure while Liberty and Colin waited in his office.<br /> <br /> Alan created a couple of dog treats full of Aether and fed one to Colin after they got back to the car. After some discussion they decide that Colin would be a good double agent and ask if he can divulge any information about the Angels.<br /> <br /> In exchange for some Aether treats, Colin tells them that his master is an Angel who wears a Hawaiian shirt and sunglasses. And that he mentioned that the Sleeper Agent Infrastructure was disrupted when the Dunkin Donuts was destroyed. But they have about thirty-five sleeper agents spread out amongst college students and homeless people. Liberty and Alan secure Colin\u2019s loyalty with promises of more Aether treats, but make sure to convince him not to tell the Angels about them or their deal.<br /> <br /> Alan and Liberty call up Ms. White and explain the situation. She is grateful and promises that she\u2019ll repay them shortly. Most likely with something to aid them in their raid of the Men in Black\u2019s HQ. Liberty calls into his work and his boss informs him that there is a plain clothes police officer staking out his work. Liberty assumes it is related to Detective Jane Bullet investigation into how he killed those Sleeper Agents. Liberty and his boss both maintain that they gave their statements to the police already so there is no need for further questions.<br /> <br /> And so we end the session with a new ally in toe and a mysterious stalker keeping an eye on Liberty. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GM Notes:</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Preparation</b>.<ul><li>Work I did before hand:<ul><li>Made XP tracker for my notes.</li> <li>Created Landing Page for my Players. This covers the NPCs they've met, goals, news stories, etc...</li> <li>Created Conspiracy Board to help visualize the conspiracy they are working against.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Session Start</b><ul><li>Two of my players showed up. Again this resulted in a bit of stagnation.</li> <li>The players took a while to catch up on what happened in previous sessions.</li> <li>I had to bring Ms. White into the picture to help get the session going.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What could I have done better:</b><ul><li>Didn't hand out any conditions this time.</li> <li>One of the players glitched, but I didn't use it.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What went well:</b><ul><li>I pulled the Infrastructure from some pre-gens I made a year ago.</li> <li>My players liked Colin and the fact they have a dog on the inside.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What do I need to not forget:</b><ul><li>Liberty Griswald<ul><li>Not much to say here. Liberty did a lot of talking to Colin, but there wasn't much new to write.</li> </ul></li> <li>Alan Thorne<ul><li>Alan's work has seen him access a secure server off work hours.</li> <li>Alan has 3 computers coming to help hack into the Men In Black HQ.</li> <li>Alan has a dog, which wasn't established before.</li> </ul></li> <li>Colin<ul><li>Colin has key information about Alan's character. And as such is a risk if he is discovered informing.</li> <li>Colin will need information to convey to the players. If he doesn't see them for a few days he may go visit Alan at work.</li> </ul></li> <li>Ms. White<ul><li>The Players have a favor to call in, but Ms. White needs something to give them for their raid.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Notes for Next Session:</b><ul><li>If Alan is able to make it to next session he may need gear.</li> <li>The raid on the Men in Black base will likely be next session.</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know what you think.</span></span><ul><li>What would be a good gadget, cover, etc... thing to give to the players from their Agency boss?</li> </ul></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEat